{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1518105197,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE0NjQ4NjU4MDY="},"added":["bug-directmode"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1518893593,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NjQ2MzA2Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2113#issuecomment-366463066"},"message":"This is because we are internally using a `diff` against `HEAD`, when doing an `add` if the new subdataset. The diff call does not work in direct mode. I happened to have a look at that today. With a more substantial RF we might be able to get a `ls-files`-based solution for this, but I am not sure whether it is worth the effort. Direct mode still has many other issues.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1518943236,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NjUwMDg3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2113#issuecomment-366500879"},"message":"I looked into this more. At the core of this issue is that we started to use `diff` to speed up path anntoation (incl. recursion). That is a good idea, but comes at the cost of direct mode issues. However, we might be able to work around, and possibly even speed up, this procedure. Here is my state of investigation:\n\nIn `add.py` there is `get_modified_subpaths()`. This is the core worker and is being called with `revision='HEAD'` in case of the call to `add` in `create`. Comparing to `HEAD` is the same functionality that is provided by `ls-files`, and in #2187 we are already using that to discover submodules.\n\nIt looks as if we could RF this code to not use `diff` in this case, and regain direct mode support for all use case like this.\n\nAlternatively, we could do this special case handling inside our `diff` implementation. Haven't looked into this possibility yet.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1518943897,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NjUwMTM0NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2113#issuecomment-366501344"},"message":"Looking into this further, I seems as if RFing `_parse_git_diff()` in `diff.py` could be a better choice. Possibly wrapping it into a general diff_helper that calls either this diff wraper or `ls-files` or something else in case of particular comparisons -- against `HEAD` being an obvious case. It is not yet clear to me how the behavior of `diff --ignore-submodules` (which is set to `none` by default) could be emulated.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1518961751,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM2NjUxNzQ0MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2113#issuecomment-366517440"},"message":"This turns out to be hard. Core issue is, as before, the implications of `--ignore-submodules=none`, which will evaluate the state of submodules, and crash if they are in direct mode (because `git status` fails).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1521531325,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3NDUwMjE3Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2113#issuecomment-374502177"},"message":"@bpoldrack you figured this all out long ago. Any chance for a fix?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1524824553,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4NDkzMDQ0MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2113#issuecomment-384930441"},"message":"I need to look into further implications, but I think it should be fixable by making use of `AnnexRepo.get_status`, which can deal with submodules in direct mode and doesn't use `git-status` but `git-annex-status`, although the functionality is somewhat limited ATM. However, I'm on the issues with direct mode again and will give it a try.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1540754665,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMzczMzgzOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2113#issuecomment-433733838"},"message":"In V6 with this one https://github.com/datalad/datalad-revolution this should no longer be an issue.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1541353528,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE5NDQ5Mjk3NTY="},"added":["waiting-for-directmode-death"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551637932,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2OTA1MDIyOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2113#issuecomment-469050228"},"message":"Direct mode? What was that?","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551637932,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjE3NjQzMjU0Mg=="},"status":2}]}